---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'SEO Areas — Birmingham & West Midlands';
const description = 'SEO Birmingham delivers local search optimisation across Birmingham city centre, Solihull, Edgbaston, Digbeth, Jewellery Quarter, Sutton Coldfield, and the wider West Midlands.';

const serviceSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'Local SEO — Birmingham and West Midlands',
  provider: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'SEO Birmingham',
    url: 'https://seo-birmingham.uk/',
    sameAs: [],
  },
  serviceType: 'Local SEO',
  areaServed: [
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Birmingham' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Edgbaston' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Digbeth' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Jewellery Quarter' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Solihull' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Sutton Coldfield' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Wolverhampton' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Coventry' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Walsall' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Dudley' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'West Bromwich' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Tamworth' },
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'Lichfield' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Bromsgrove' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Colmore Business District' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Brindleyplace' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Birmingham Business Park, Solihull' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Innovation Birmingham Campus' },
    { '@type': 'Place', name: 'Custard Factory' },
  ],
};

const faqData = [
  {
    question: 'Do you work outside Birmingham city centre?',
    answer: 'We cover the entire West Midlands. Solihull, Wolverhampton, Coventry, Walsall, Dudley, Tamworth, Lichfield, Bromsgrove — each area gets a strategy built from its own competitive data and search demand. Not a copy-paste job.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Why does local SEO differ across Birmingham districts?',
    answer: 'Every district has its own business mix, competitive density, and customer search behaviour. A solicitor in Colmore Business District faces completely different local rivals to a trades business in Sutton Coldfield. Google weights proximity, relevance, and prominence differently depending on query and location. That demands area-specific tactics.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How do you handle multi-location campaigns in the West Midlands?',
    answer: 'We build dedicated landing pages for each location. Optimise individual Google Business Profiles. Develop area-specific citations. Produce content targeting the terms customers in each area actually use. This avoids the thin-content trap that generic multi-location pages create.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Where is SEO competition fiercest in Birmingham?',
    answer: 'Colmore Business District and city centre are the hardest markets for professional services SEO. The Jewellery Quarter is brutal for jewellery and retail queries. Solihull runs hot for property, automotive, and professional services. Suburban areas like Sutton Coldfield and Bromsgrove offer faster wins — less competition, quicker results.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you help businesses that serve the whole West Midlands?',
    answer: 'Yes. For regional businesses, we build a hub-and-spoke content architecture. Establish authority in Birmingham first, then extend visibility to surrounding towns and cities. This captures broad West Midlands terms and hyper-local queries in each area.',
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqData.map((faq) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: faq.question,
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: faq.answer,
    },
  })),
};
---

<Base title={title} description={description} schema={[serviceSchema, faqSchema]}>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 prose">
    <h1>SEO Coverage Across Birmingham and the West Midlands</h1>

    <div class="quick-answer">
      <strong>Quick answer:</strong> We run local SEO across Birmingham city centre, Solihull, Edgbaston, Digbeth, the Jewellery Quarter, Sutton Coldfield, and the wider West Midlands. Every area strategy is built from local search data and competitive intelligence — not guesswork.
    </div>

    <section>
      <p>Birmingham is not one market. It is a collection of distinct commercial districts, each with its own industry mix, customer base, and competitive intensity. Colmore Business District plays nothing like Digbeth. Sutton Coldfield plays nothing like Solihull. A single uniform strategy fails here.</p>

      <p>We deliver SEO across every major Birmingham district and surrounding West Midlands town. Each engagement starts with local data: what customers in that area search for, who dominates right now, and where the gaps are. From there we build the technical infrastructure, citations, content, and authority signals needed to win visibility in that specific market.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Birmingham City Centre</h2>

      <p>The commercial heart of the West Midlands. The most competitive local SEO environment in the region. Professional services firms, retailers, hospitality operators, and tech companies all fight for the same eyeballs. The local pack is heavily contested — especially for solicitors, accountants, and financial advisors.</p>

      <p>Winning here demands a polished Google Business Profile, airtight NAP consistency, and content that screams Birmingham relevance. Businesses near the Bullring and Grand Central benefit from association with high-authority landmarks in local signals. We combine local and organic SEO for maximum aggregate visibility. Full details on our <a href="/services/">SEO services</a> page.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Birmingham Districts</h2>

      <h3>Edgbaston</h3>
      <p>One of Birmingham's wealthiest suburbs. Home to Queen Elizabeth Hospital and the Edgbaston Medical Quarter, private schools, and high-end professional services. SEO competition is moderate but climbing — especially for medical, dental, and wellness queries. Residents have high disposable income and specific expectations.</p>

      <h3>Digbeth</h3>
      <p>Birmingham's creative and cultural quarter. The Custard Factory and Zellig anchor a district packed with tech startups, creative agencies, and hospitality ventures. SEO here targets younger demographics and emerging brands with thin domain authority. Content-led strategies and social signals carry more weight than in traditional commercial districts.</p>

      <h3>Jewellery Quarter</h3>
      <p>Roughly 40% of UK jewellery production happens here. Over 500 trade businesses. SEO competition for jewellery terms is fierce — independents slug it out with national brands. Success requires product-level structured data, image optimisation for visual search, and content proving genuine craft expertise. E-commerce SEO and Google Shopping are essential.</p>

      <h3>Solihull</h3>
      <p>Sits where Birmingham's commercial reach meets the affluent commuter belt. Birmingham Business Park hosts major corporates. The town centre sustains strong independent retail and professional services. SEO strategies target both Solihull itself and the broader South Birmingham corridor. Property, automotive, and professional services are the hottest verticals.</p>

      <h3>Sutton Coldfield</h3>
      <p>A distinct market within Birmingham's search landscape. Royal Town status and suburban character produce search behaviour skewed toward local services, trades, and family businesses. Competition is lower than city centre. That creates opportunity for businesses that move decisively on local SEO. Google Business Profile optimisation and Sutton-specific content deliver strong returns.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Wider West Midlands Coverage</h2>

      <p>We cover the full West Midlands conurbation. Each town has its own search dynamics. We adjust accordingly.</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Wolverhampton</strong> — Strong manufacturing and retail base. Digital economy expanding. SEO competition rising for professional services and trades.</li>
        <li><strong>Coventry</strong> — University city with a growing tech sector. City of Culture legacy keeps tourism and hospitality search demand elevated.</li>
        <li><strong>Walsall</strong> — Historic leather goods manufacturing pivoting to modern retail and services. Lower SEO competition means quick wins for proactive businesses.</li>
        <li><strong>Dudley</strong> — Tourism draws (Black Country Living Museum, Dudley Zoo) plus established trades and manufacturing chasing local visibility.</li>
        <li><strong>West Bromwich</strong> — Growing commercial centre. Rising demand for professional services SEO and local search for retail.</li>
        <li><strong>Tamworth</strong> — Commuter town with a solid local business community. Low competitive density. Businesses that commit to SEO early win fast.</li>
        <li><strong>Lichfield</strong> — Cathedral city, affluent demographics. Professional services, independent retail, and hospitality compete for a discerning audience.</li>
        <li><strong>Bromsgrove</strong> — Straddles Birmingham and Worcestershire. Local businesses gain from targeting both Birmingham-adjacent and Bromsgrove-specific search terms.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Birmingham Business Hubs</h2>

      <p>Several dedicated hubs within Birmingham demand targeted SEO strategies due to sheer commercial density.</p>

      <h3>Colmore Business District</h3>
      <p>Birmingham's premier financial and professional services quarter. Major banks, law firms, accountancy practices, corporate HQs. SEO competition here is the fiercest in the region. You need serious domain authority, clear E-E-A-T signals, and content that proves expertise — or you do not rank.</p>

      <h3>Brindleyplace</h3>
      <p>Mixed commercial and leisure development. Strong brand recognition in local search. Hospitality operators contest dining and leisure terms. Professional services firms target corporate keywords. The area's identity works for you if you optimise around it.</p>

      <h3>Birmingham Business Park</h3>
      <p>One of the UK's largest business parks, based in Solihull. Tech, logistics, and professional services tenants. SEO often targets national terms, but a local layer captures substantial Solihull and South Birmingham demand.</p>

      <h3>Innovation Birmingham Campus</h3>
      <p>The city's primary tech and innovation hub. Startups, scale-ups, R&D operations. SEO centres on SaaS keywords, B2B lead generation, and thought leadership content that builds authority in emerging sectors.</p>

      <h3>Custard Factory</h3>
      <p>Digbeth's creative hub. Independent businesses, agencies, makers. SEO here leans on brand building, content marketing, and social visibility alongside traditional search tactics.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Why Local SEO Varies by Area</h2>

      <p>Google's local algorithm weighs three things: proximity (how close the searcher is to your business), relevance (how well your listing matches the query), and prominence (how established and authoritative you are). These factors play out differently in every Birmingham area.</p>

      <p>In dense zones like Colmore Business District, proximity matters less — dozens of similar businesses cluster together. Prominence and relevance decide winners. Stronger reviews, more authoritative citations, better content. In suburban areas like Sutton Coldfield, proximity carries more weight. Solid foundational SEO lets you dominate your patch.</p>

      <p>We analyse these dynamics for every area we serve. Running identical tactics in Wolverhampton and the Jewellery Quarter would waste money — the competition, the customer, and the search intent are materially different. That is why our <a href="/services/">SEO services</a> always start with data from your specific area.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="cta-box">
      <h2 style="color: white; margin-top: 0;">Own Your Local Search</h2>
      <p>City centre, suburbs, or wider West Midlands — we build the local SEO strategy that puts you in front of customers searching in your market.</p>
      <a href="/contact/">Talk to Us</a>
    </div>

    <section class="faq-section">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      {faqData.map((faq) => (
        <details>
          <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
